.TH CCOL_CHAN_RECV_ZC 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
ccol_chan_recv_zc \- receive a message from the ccol_channel (blocking)
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <cthreadcomm.h>

ccol_retval_t ccol_chan_recv_zc(ccol_channel *ch, c_message_t *target_buf);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Automatically selects the appropriate queue based on calling thread:
- Owner thread receives from workers_to_owner queue
- Worker threads receive from owner_to_workers queue

Blocks until a message arrives and transfers ownership.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
ch          Channel to receive from
target_buf  Buffer to receive the message (receives ownership of data)
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
ccol_success       - Message received (caller must free target_buf->data)
ccol_invalid_args  - ch or target_buf is NULL
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
Blocks until a message arrives in the selected queue
Direction is automatically determined by thread ID
Caller receives ownership of target_buf->data and must free it
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR ccol_chan_try_recv_zc (3),
.BR ccol_chan_timed_recv_zc (3),
.BR ccol_chan_send_zc (3)
